{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And his heart grew faint.</b> From the root of \"do not let a tear stop for yourself\" (Lamentations 2:18). The sense is that his heart and blood stood still, as in the sense of \"and his heart died\" (1 Samuel 25:37), for he did not believe. And when he saw the wagons his spirit revived. Do not wonder at the word ויפג, for so is the way of the prophets to speak, as in \"and no breath was left in me\" (Daniel 10:17)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "The root citation from Lamentations uses פוגת (a stopping/ceasing); Ibn Ezra spells it with a tav rather than the standard פוגה."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:05.725195350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}